lessons.math.push(chapter('Gradients and complex differentiability','The gradient points in the direction of maximum local increase. Project it onto a unit direction to obtain the directional derivative. For a complex function, differentiability is stronger than it is for functions of two real variables. The Cauchy–Riemann equations relate the real and imaginary partial derivatives.',['grad','cc'],'For f=x²+y² at (1,2), the gradient is (2,4). Its component along the positive x-axis is 2.','A directional derivative uses a unit direction. An unnormalized vector also scales the result.'));
